# Astra Game Launcher Workspace Rules

## Git Automation
After generating, modifying, or fixing code:
1. Review the changes with `git status` and `git diff`
2. Stage changes: `git add .`
3. Commit with a descriptive message: `git commit -m "feat: description"` or `git commit -m "fix: description"`
4. Push to the current branch: `git push origin HEAD`
5. Always push unless explicitly told "don't commit yet"

## Branch Naming
- Feature branches: `feat/feature-name`
- Bug fixes: `fix/bug-name`
- Refactoring: `refactor/component-name`
- Documentation: `docs/what-changed`

## Commit Message Format
- `feat: add new feature` (new functionality)
- `fix: resolve bug in X` (bug fix)
- `refactor: simplify component Y` (code improvement)
- `docs: update README` (documentation)

## Project Context
- **Type:** Electron + React 19 Game Launcher
- **Frontend:** React, TypeScript, Vite
- **Backend:** Electron IPC, Node.js
- **Main Repo:** https://github.com/[USERNAME]/astra-game-launcher
- **Reviewer:** Claude (via GitHub MCP integration)

## When Reviewer Asks for Changes
1. Make the requested modifications
2. Commit and push to the same branch
3. Claude will fetch the updated branch automatically
